  "answer": "According to the MedlinePlus summary on Rosacea, skin symptoms include frequent facial redness or flushing, small red lines under the skin, acne, a swollen nose, and thick skin on the forehead, chin, and cheeks. Eye symptoms can involve red, dry, itchy eyes and sometimes vision problems. The provided text does not state an exact percentage of people with rosacea who develop eye symptoms or vision problems."
